From 58c42c3c8ac2ec58f5499b86bc3ad49b05fe992f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Ga=C3=ABl=20Duval?= <gael@murena.io>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 23:03:20 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] feat(libfont): substitute missing fonts the way Word does

When a font is not installed, the replacement was chosen only by
panose/metrics similarity against the installed fonts, so Calibri
reached Carlito only by chance, and any font missing from the built-in
dictionary (Andika, Marianne, school fonts...) fell back to Liberation
Sans, while Word uses its default font Calibri.

GetSubstituteName (used by GetFontFile/GetFontFileWeb) now resolves the
name first:
- an installed font with the requested name always wins (real fonts on
  a Windows desktop with Office);
- otherwise the first installed font of an ordered table of
  metric-compatible clones (Carlito, Caladea, Liberation, Gelasio,
  URW Gothic, Comic Relief, Archivo Black, Selawik, P052...);
- otherwise, for a font unknown to the font dictionary, Word's default
  font Calibri (hence Carlito when Calibri is missing);
- otherwise the existing dictionary/penalty matching.

Measured with Word for the web references: unknown fonts are rendered
in Calibri by Word (a01, a09, t01, t05, t06 of our corpus).

Test: tests/common/libfont/fontSubstitution.html.

[upstreamable]

Assisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5
